[{"id":"4028034","question":"Will NYC have more than 6 inches of precipitation in September?","conditionId":"0x80cfbda7d19183b6206dd6fefb18cbf0f5877d0f528c422c4dd4897c4c302779","slug":"will-nyc-have-more-than-6-inches-of-precipitation-in-september","resolutionSource":"","endDate":"2026-09-30T23:59:00Z","liquidity":"155.96","startDate":"2026-08-31T13:44:17Z","image":"https://polymarket-upload.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/will-nyc-have-more-than-75-inches-of-snowfall-on-tuesday-694eec22-7ccf-46ff-bd54-d2695af8a636.png","icon":"https://polymarket-upload.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/will-nyc-have-more-than-75-inches-of-snowfall-on-tuesday-694eec22-7ccf-46ff-bd54-d2695af8a636.png","description":"This market will resolve according to the total precipitation in inches in Central Park, New York City between September 1 and September 30, 2026, 11:59PM ET according to the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA).\n\nIf the reported value falls exactly between two brackets, then this market will resolve to the higher range bracket.\n\nThe resolution source for this market will be NOAA, specifically the figure for September 2026 when the \"Monthly summarized data\" for \"Central Park NY\" is selected with the variable set to \"Precipitation\" at the https://www.weather.gov/wrh/climate?wfo=okx link once that figure is finalized for the whole month of September 2026.\n\nIf the relevant data is not available by December 7, 2026, 11:59 PM ET, another credible resolution source will be chosen.\n\nThe resolution source for this market measures precipitation to 2 decimal places (e.g., 1.54), thus, this is the level of precision that will be used when resolving this market. Any revisions to precipitation recorded after data is finalized for this market's timeframe will not be considered for this market's resolution.","outcomes":"[\"Yes\", \"No\"]","outcomePrices":"[\"0.195\", \"0.805\"]","volume":"45","active":true,"closed":false,"marketMakerAddress":"","createdAt":"2026-08-3